{"findings":[{"finding":"The spec says it overrides accepted assumption ASM-24 (Stripe card payments) and switches to staff recording payments by hand, which contradicts an assumption the human accepted.","reqId":"REQ-74","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Order emails always go to the 'Buyer who placed the order', with no rule for when that Buyer is deactivated or moved to another company (AC-16.4), so company A's order details could be emailed to a Fleet Co user.","reqId":"REQ-47","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"REQ-2 hides whether an account exists behind one identical 401, but REQ-3 returns 423 'locked' only for real accounts and AC-4.1 returns 403 'account is inactive', so either response reveals that the email is registered.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-25 prices every basket line from the price list current 'at the time of the request', yet REQ-42/AC-42.2 rejects submission because a line was 're-priced'; that only makes sense if the basket stores the price from when the line was added, which REQ-25 rules out.","reqId":"REQ-42","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-44 stores a copy of the delivery address on the order, but REQ-57 still refuses to confirm when the original address 'no longer exists', so staff removing an address (AC-82.3) blocks confirmation of every Received order that used it.","reqId":"REQ-80","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No requirement or acceptance criterion says what happens when a Buyer submits an empty basket, or one with no delivery address or no delivery date selected.","reqId":"REQ-44","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff may remove lines from a Received order, but nothing stops them removing the last line, which would leave an order with no lines that can still be confirmed and invoiced.","reqId":"REQ-55","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Confirmation checks stock, retired products and the address, but not whether the requested delivery date has already passed or is no longer valid (for example after a settings change).","reqId":"REQ-57","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is defined for retiring a category that still has active products: are they hidden, uncategorised or still shown under the filter, and is retiring blocked?","reqId":"REQ-76","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Deactivating a price list that is assigned to companies has no acceptance criterion or error path, even though, per the spec's assumption, every product for those companies becomes 'Price on request' and ordering stops.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Invitations have no error path for an email that already belongs to an existing account, or for inviting a Buyer into an inactive company.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Admins can change roles and deactivate users, but nothing stops them demoting or deactivating the last remaining Administrator, including themselves.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Password reset and invitation acceptance set no password rules (rejecting empty or weak passwords) and do not say whether the user's other sessions are ended after a reset.","reqId":"REQ-10","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says whether a password reset works for a Pending (invited) account, which could let someone activate it without the invitation link, or for a deactivated account.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"There is no way to reverse or correct an invoice marked paid by mistake; once Paid, every further action returns 409 ALREADY_PAID.","reqId":"REQ-74","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"A repeated order merging into a basket that already holds the same product has no rule for adding the quantities together and capping the total at stock.","reqId":"REQ-52","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Changing a Buyer's company (AC-16.4) does not say what happens to their open session's basket (priced from the old company's list, possibly with the old company's address) or to their past orders.","reqId":"REQ-16","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-3.4 checks that 'the account record lock field is empty', which is internal storage and not visible through any API response.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-28.1 and AC-28.3 check database 'row' counts on the price list rather than an API response; AC-80.1 ('company row') and AC-61.2 ('order row stores the reason') do the same.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-35.1 depends on recording network traffic to 'the ERP host', which no public endpoint exposes, and it clashes with reading the file over SFTP (ASM-7) if the ERP host is the file location.","reqId":"REQ-35","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Import rows are matched on distributor product code and checked against fixed 'required columns', even though ASM-7 says the client will supply the column layout, so the column names and matching key should be configurable.","reqId":"REQ-31","rubric":8,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The spec fixes 'one currency with 2 decimal places' but the settings list in REQ-83 has no currency setting, so the currency shown on prices, invoices and PDFs is hardcoded and never named.","reqId":"REQ-81","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Dashboard counts of failed stock imports (REQ-67, REQ-69) are neither order queues nor delivery information (I-6), and these low-stability requirements add dashboard features beyond what was asked.","reqId":"REQ-67","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The PDF has to show 'no tax lines' because the spec picked ASM-50, but the accepted ASM-23 says the invoice shows VAT at a configurable rate; the spec settles this payments conflict with its own 'later wins' rule instead of asking the human.","reqId":"REQ-111","rubric":1,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"Working days exclude 'configured public holidays' (ASM-49), which directly contradicts the accepted ASM-19 ('no holiday list in phase 1'); the spec resolves this itself rather than asking.","reqId":"REQ-112","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing says what happens when the ERP file is missing from the configured location, can't be read, or is the same file already imported the night before; only empty files and missing headers are covered (REQ-13).","reqId":"REQ-95","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"For duplicate product codes it is unclear whether every duplicate row is rejected or only the second one, and no AC covers duplicates, so the stock value that ends up applied is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-96","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No behaviour is given for a report requested without a date range or with start after end (ASM-7 was never actually answered), and there is no error status for these cases.","reqId":"REQ-87","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Nothing covers a customer with no assigned price list, or a product that isn't on the customer's price list, when viewing or ordering.","reqId":"REQ-113","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"'Authorised user' is never defined, and no AC checks that a user from another customer, or an unauthenticated caller, is denied GET /invoices/{id}/pdf, even though the risk tags include PII.","reqId":"REQ-111","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"There is no validation path for a missing, future-dated, or earlier-than-invoice-date payment date on mark-paid.","reqId":"REQ-110","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Sign-in failure is only handled through a generic message; there is no rate limiting or lockout for repeated failed attempts, despite the auth risk tag.","reqId":"REQ-102","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only expiry is covered; nothing says what happens when a reset or invitation token is reused after it has already been consumed, or is tampered with.","reqId":"REQ-103","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Rolling back the business action when the audit write fails is undefined for the 'ERP import failed' audit in REQ-15: there is no successful action to roll back, and the import status record could be lost.","reqId":"REQ-123","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-25.2 only says 'the response is an error' and doesn't give an observable status code or body.","reqId":"REQ-108","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The requirement refers to 'the listed customer, staff and admin screens', but the spec never lists them, so the AC can't be checked against a defined set.","reqId":"REQ-119","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The requirement says status is shown on the System/Import status screen, but AC-15.1 only checks the GET /admin/imports API and labels the test as job level, so the screen itself is never verified.","reqId":"REQ-98","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 10 MB upload limit and the allowed file types are hard-coded in the requirement, while similar limits (link lifetimes, cut-off, payment term) are configuration.","reqId":"REQ-118","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The daily overdue job's run time and timezone are not specified, so the boundary for 'has passed' (for example, exactly 30 days) is ambiguous.","reqId":"REQ-109","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-6.3 demands a separate QA 'Customer data-isolation testing' row with its own effort values, but AC-1.1/NFR-3 fix QA at exactly 12 rows, each named after a section-74 checklist item, so an extra row the checklist doesn't name breaks the count.","reqId":"REQ-129","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Staff manage companies but only admins manage users (Q-5), and nothing says how a new company's customer users get accounts (admin-only creation, staff request, or invitation), so the onboarding and permission path behind the 'User management' and 'Customer management' rows is undefined.","reqId":"REQ-129","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"ASM-8 blocks quantities above stock with a message, but nothing says whether that check applies to staff amendments or staff-created orders, so the over-stock path is undefined for the amendment and staff order rows.","reqId":"REQ-128","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Cancellation and amendment both stop at dispatch and the invoice is created at dispatch, but no row covers correcting a dispatched or invoiced order (credit note, return or void), so the post-dispatch error path is missing from the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-131","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Risk tags include pii, yet keeping order and invoice records indefinitely (ASM-13) comes with no path for anonymising or erasing customer-user personal data, and no row or proposal section covers it.","reqId":"REQ-135","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-10.3's 'no row in the estimate depends on an open question that is missing from the list' can't be checked, because there's no reference list of open questions to compare against (ASM-1 says the section was never supplied).","reqId":"REQ-133","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The estimate depends on volume (ASM-18/24), hosting (ASM-19/25), retention (ASM-13) and daily pickup (Q-8), but AC-10.1/10.2 don't list them, while AC-10.3 requires every unconfirmed dependency to appear, so the enumerated lists are incomplete against the AC's own rule.","reqId":"REQ-133","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The ERP pickup frequency is fixed at 'daily' in the scoped row, and the spec explicitly drops ASM-5's configurable frequency, so a schedule value that belongs in configuration is baked into the estimate.","reqId":"REQ-132","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-13.1 requires the proposal to name one specific cloud region, which hardcodes a deployment identifier that should be the client's configurable choice within their own account.","reqId":"REQ-136","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-12.2 requires the proposal to name a backup approach, but backup isn't one of the 10 section-75 areas listed in REQ-11, which goes beyond the requested proposal scope.","reqId":"REQ-135","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"'Assumptions used' is never pinned to a defined set, and REQ-10 has its own numbered entries rather than ASM IDs, so a reviewer can't measure '100% cited by ID' against a fixed denominator.","reqId":"NFR-2","rubric":3,"severity":"low"}],"note":"No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer) No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer) No OpenAI key: critic ran on claude-opus-5-5 (same family as the implementer)"}